## SQ-CMP-01 | Compat loads, mixins apply once
@group A
@commands `grep -E "\[creativecompat\]\|creativecompat.mixins.json" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c "from creativecompat.mixins.json" logs/debug.log`
@pass Compat core line; no mixin apply error; the 27 common mixins apply on the server (minus any whose mod is absent)
@fails Jar missing, a gate id wrong in `CompatMixinPlugin`, or Creative Common still listing a moved mixin (applied twice)
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
bootexpect \[creativecompat\] loaded \(config/
bootreject creativecompat\.mixins\.json.*(Error|error|failed)
shell grep -c "from creativecompat.mixins.json" logs/debug.log; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]* from creativecompat.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sort -u | wc -l; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]* from creativecompat.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sed 's/Mixing //;s/ from.*//' | sort -u > /tmp/cmp_mx.txt; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]* from creativeengineering.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sed 's/Mixing //;s/ from.*//' | sort -u | comm -12 - /tmp/cmp_mx.txt | head; rm -f /tmp/cmp_mx.txt
look up to 27 common mixins from creativecompat.mixins.json; none also from creativeengineering.mixins.json (the comm list above is empty)

## SQ-CMP-02 | config sections carried to the Compat file
@group A
@commands Same boot: read `config/creativecompat-common.toml`, `config/creativeengineering-common.toml`; restart, grep again
@pass `[swaps] config sections [leaf_piles, moss, vine_shearing, campfire, monster_box, trash_slot] carried over`; Compat file holds the edited `rainOutTicks`; the CE file no longer has the six sections after the boot; second boot no WARN
@fails `carrySections` ran after config load, or Forge did not correct the CE file
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
@superseded legacy config from 1.1.06, migration shipped in 1.2.00 and already ran on both machines (owner, 2026-11-18)
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[leaf_piles, moss, vine_shearing, campfire, monster_box, trash_slot\] carried over
shell grep -n "rainOutTicks" config/creativecompat-common.toml; grep -nE "^\s*\[(leaf_piles|moss|vine_shearing|campfire|monster_box|trash_slot)\]" config/creativeengineering-common.toml || echo "CE has none of the six"
look Compat file rainOutTicks = 200; CE file lost the six sections (restart half in cs2_boot2b)

## SQ-CMP-03 | Compat startup pack, item physics
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "startup script packs in order\|creativecompat" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass Pack `creativecompat` loads; no `[creativecompat] global.itemPhysics missing` error; item physics rules load (count line as before)
@fails Startup tree not in the jar, or the ItemPhysic class names in `item_physics.js` wrong
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
shell grep -E "startup script packs in order|creativecompat|item_physics" logs/kubejs/startup.log | cut -c1-220 | head -8
kjsreject global\.itemPhysics missing|ItemPhysicSplit not on classpath
look pack creativecompat loads; [item_physics] summary line as before

## SQ-CMP-04 | /dumpphysics
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/dumpphysics` (Devtools)
@pass Runs and lists rules (it loads `com.SaintAlfonzo.creativecompat.itemphysic.ItemPhysicSplit`)
@fails dump_physics.js class name
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
> dumpphysics
sleep 5
reject Unknown or incomplete command
reject (Error|Exception)
look rules listed

## SQ-CMP-05 | TNT item in fire, fireproof item in lava
@group A
@commands Same boot: throw a TNT-tagged item into fire (an item burn rule with shrapnel); throw a fireproof item into lava
@pass Blast plus shrapnel as before; fireproof item survives
@fails `BurnBursts` handler not registered by the shrapnel side
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
# self-contained since r1118 (judge-5, 2026-11-18): the {H} home marker came from a lost setup row; fixed superflat spot
> forceload add 200 200 232 232
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome] run summon minecraft:marker 200 -60 200 {Tags:["cmphome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome,limit=1] Pos
capture H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {H1+20} {H3+20}
sleep 5
# items of the same kind merge: clear earlier test items first
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x={H1+22},y={H2},z={H3+20},distance=..30]
> setblock {H1+20} {H2-1} {H3+20} minecraft:netherrack
> setblock {H1+20} {H2} {H3+20} minecraft:fire
> setblock {H1+24} {H2-1} {H3+20} minecraft:stone
> setblock {H1+24} {H2} {H3+20} minecraft:lava
> summon minecraft:item {H1+20} {H2+1} {H3+20} {Item:{id:"minecraft:tnt",Count:1b},Tags:["cmp_tnt2"]}
> summon minecraft:item {H1+24} {H2+1} {H3+20} {Item:{id:"minecraft:netherite_ingot",Count:1b},Tags:["cmp_fp2"]}
sleep 15
> execute if block {H1+20} {H2} {H3+20} minecraft:fire run say CMP fire still burning
> execute unless entity @e[type=item,tag=cmp_tnt2] run say CMP tnt item burned
> execute if entity @e[type=item,tag=cmp_fp2] run say CMP fireproof item survived
expect CMP tnt item burned
expect CMP fireproof item survived
shell grep -iE "shrapnel|burnExplode|BurnBursts" logs/latest.log | tail -3 | cut -c1-200
look the blast itself is not visible on a console; the TNT item is consumed and the netherite stays

## SQ-CMP-06 | weathered cardboard box, monster box loot, physics tags
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/give` a weathered cardboard box and place it; `/loot` the monster box reward table; check `#creativeengineering:...` physics tags with `/dumptags`
@pass Block and item exist (`creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box`); loot table resolves; physics tags present
@fails Startup `decor_blocks.js` or jar data paths
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
# self-contained since r1118 (judge-5, 2026-11-18; ids creativecompat: since the 2026-11-09 move): the {H} home marker came from a lost setup row; fixed superflat spot
> forceload add 200 200 232 232
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome] run summon minecraft:marker 200 -60 200 {Tags:["cmphome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome,limit=1] Pos
capture H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> execute unless entity qa run pbot spawn qa {H1} {H2} {H3} minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> setblock {H1+8} {H2} {H3} creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box
> execute if block {H1+8} {H2} {H3} creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box run say CMP box placed
> give qa creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box
> loot give qa loot creativecompat:misc/monster_box_reward
expect CMP box placed
reject Unknown (block|item)|Unknown loot table
> dumptags
waitlog (dumptags|tags).*(done|written|wrote) 300
shell python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/tags/item_tags_by_item.json'));print({k:len(v) for k,v in d.items() if 'cardboard' in k})" 2>&1 | cut -c1-300; ls kubejs/exported/tags/ | head
look block, item and loot resolve; physics tags present

## SQ-CMP-07 | paintings
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -ciE "paintings" logs/latest.log`; Immersive Paintings painting list count (the pack's 475 images)
@pass Same count as before the carve; no painting load error
@fails Paintings not loaded from a mod jar datapack (move them back to the pack folder)
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
shell grep -ciE "paintings" logs/latest.log; grep -iE "immersive_?paintings" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "error|fail|load" | head -3 | cut -c1-200; ls kubejs/data | head -40 | tr '\n' ' '
look painting count as before the carve, no load error

## SQ-CMP-08 | moved server scripts, /reload
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "Error occurred while handling event\|creativecompat" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log \| head`; `/reload`
@pass No script error from the moved server files (coin, starter kit, feature ports, flowers, misc mods, tag rows); `/reload` clean
@fails A moved script reading a top-level name from the pack's scope
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
shell grep -E "Error occurred while handling event|creativecompat" logs/kubejs/server.log | head -6 | cut -c1-220; grep -c "Error occurred while handling event" logs/latest.log; true
kjsreject Error occurred while handling event
> reload
waitlog (Reloaded|reload) 180
sleep 10
shell grep -cE "Error occurred while handling event|ReferenceError" logs/kubejs/server.log; true
look no script error from moved Compat files; /reload clean

